Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||10-04-2001||10:20 PM||||i was searching for info on chopping the top of my gt and came up with a pretty neat idea... although i need a few second opinions on if its possible/safe and maybe a few suggestions. Heres my idea and how I would accomplish it.<BR>3" chop top with a targa covertible top, custom make all the new windows and top with plexiglass(or lexan? just read about it on v8archie's site) add in a roll cage for added protection. I'm just not sure if cutting the roof frame will do some damage to the strength of the fiero's frame. a chop top roadster would be amazing and definitly a one of a kind. Anyway, give me some feedback!||||reg||6
Z||000001||Devotshka||10-04-2001||11:33 PM||||If you are going to make it a Targa top you will need to reinforce the frame from below.  <P>If you just lower the roofline i don't think you need a permanent reinforcement, just while the roof is cut until you weld it back together... i may be wrong on that one though, never seen any choptops being done.<P>||||reg||3
